{{Culture of Balisca}}

'''''Desconexión''''' is an [[Baliscano language|Baliscano]] word that roughly translates as "disconnection" or "unplugging". This term is used to describe a widespread [[Balisca|Baliscan]] [[w:counterculture|counter]]/{{W|subculture}} known for its strongly {{W|anti-authority|anti-authority}}, [[W:Anarchism#Evolutionary|evolutionary]] and {{W|social anarchism|social anarchist}} ideals. It has become associated with the {{W|NEET}} demographic, of which youth make up a disproportionate percentage. While often labelled "{{W|hippie}}", it originated in the [[Special Period]]-era hardships faced by the overwhelmingly young [[w:NEET|NEET]] Baliscans struggling with social and economic struggles (particularly [[Baliscan housing shortage|housing insecurity]]) in [[Araucaria]] and other areas of the confederation.

Desconexión is considered a uniquely Baliscan phenomenon, pairing the {{W|grunge}}, {{W|beatnik}}, {{W|hippie}} and {{W|Sumak kawsay|buen vivir}} concepts with rebel movements from past eras with the {{W|Anarcho-naturism|their rejection}} of today’s {{W|industrialisation|industrialized}} {{W|mass society}}. It draws significant inspiration from the diverse cultural and ethnic background of the Baliscan Confederation, reflecting the misfortune of communities left behind by the country's rapid socioeconomic transformation. In contemporary Baliscan society it has increasingly dominated over more Illypnian and [[w:Bohemian style|Bohemian]] influences that are typically dominant in the rest of the world. It's rapid rise into mainstream Baliscan society has led to a blending of beauty and fashion trends from across the world, leading to occasional accusations of [[w:Cultural appropriation|cultural appropriation]]. Desconexión is closely associated with {{W|Permissive society|permissive}} beliefs, such as [[w:Sexual revolution|sexual liberation]], {{W|free love}}, {{W|post-genderism}}, {{W|anarchist egoism|egoism}}, {{W|anti-statism}}, {{W|recreational drug use}}, and {{W|Dealignment|political dealignment}}.

Desconexión accelerated the Baliscan {{W|Critique of work|anti-work movement}} and has embraced tenets of [[W:Illegalism|illegalism]], which has also fueled illicit activity including [[Baliscan Mafia|Mafia-related]] crime and [[Cybercrime in Balisca|cybercrime]]. It played a significant role in the [[2021 Baliscan civil unrest]], and influenced the push for the recognition of [[autonomous commune (Balisca)|autonomous commune]]s.

Baliscans that subscribe to desconexión actively choose to lower their professional and economic ambitions and simplify their goals, still being fiscally responsible for their own essential needs, and prioritize psychological health over [[W:Economic materialism|economic materialism]]. There is a strong criticism of [[W:Wage slavery|wage slavery]] and such, the desconexión movement has been blamed as the main driver of Balisca's high youth unemployment rate.

