===Fashion===
{{Main|Baliscan streetwear}}Desconexión is actively opposed to [[W:fast fashion|fast fashion]] for several reasons, particularly sustainability concerns and to protest the industry's extensive exploitation of [[W:Third world|third world]] [[W:Child workers|child workers]] in [[W:Sweat shops|sweatshops]] to produce clothing cheaply for large profits. Instead embracing [[W:Thrift store chic|thrifting]], [[W:Upcycling|upcycling]] and traditional methods such as [[W:Sewing|sewing]] and [[W:Patchwork|patchwork]]. 

Stereotypical fashion elements include {{W|unisex clothing}}, {{W|vintage fashion|vintage clothes}}, {{W|alternative fashion|alternative}} and {{W|genderqueer fashion}}, {{W|streetwear}}, or a mixture of different fashions, often including {{W|skinny jeans}}, {{W|dress shirt|button-up shirts}}, {{W|crop tops}}, a full beards/facial hair, {{W|mullet}}s, {{W|Natural hair movement|natural hair}} styles such as {{W|dreads|locs}}, {{W|cornrows}} and {{W|box braids}} that are typically viewed as unkempt in other western societies, and thick-rimmed or lensless glasses.

