==Ideologies==
{{See also|Baliscan values}}
[[File:Flag of Yippies.svg|300px|thumb|left|The flag of the [[Nobody Party]], a {{W|joke party}} that is closely aligned with Desconexión. They are well known for {{W|street theatre}}, {{W|dirtbag left|dirtbag}} commentary and politically themed pranks.]]
Political and socioeconomic ideologies associated with desconexión are mostly concerned with individual freedom and {{W|anti-establishment}} views. Common viewpoints include [[w:Civil liberties|individual liberty]], {{W|anti-authoritarianism}}, a {{W|DIY ethic}}, non-conformity, anti-{{W|corporatism}}, anti-government, {{W|direct action}} and not "{{W|selling out}}".

Centering on a belief in the {{W|Absurdism|abject lack of meaning and value to life}}, {{W|hedonism}} and {{W|egoism}} have become fixtures of desconexión. As such, followers of the movement are described as having a "{{W|All work and no play makes Jack a dull boy|all play and no work}}" mentality, and have been known to seek entertainment wherever they can and maximize {{W|leisure}}. This is often manifested in {{W|recreational drug use}}.
[[File:October 73 riots.png|thumb|251x251px|Youth-led [[October 76|civil unrest]] during the [[Special Period]].]]
''Desconexiónistas'' universally believe in {{W|direct action}}, although the way in which this manifests itself varies greatly. Many desconexiónistas are [[w:pacifism|pacifists]] and therefore believe in using non-violent means of achieving their aims. These include {{W|nonviolent resistance}}, {{W|refusal of work}}, {{W|squatting}}, economic {{W|sabotage}}, {{W|dumpster diving}}, {{W|graffiti}}, {{W|culture jamming}}, {{W|ecotage}}, {{W|freeganism}}, {{W|boycott}}ing, {{W|civil disobedience}}, {{W|hacktivism}} and {{W|subvertising}}. However, it is agreed amongst desconexiónistas that [[W:Destruction of property|property damage]] is a natural form of expression. This manifests itself as {{W|riot}}ing, {{W|vandalism}}, wire cutting, {{W|ecotage}}, [[w:Hunt saboteur|hunt sabotage]], participation in {{W|Animal Liberation Front}}, {{W|Earth Liberation Front|Adonia Liberation Front}}, or even {{W|Black Bloc}} and {{W|Antifa}} style activities, and in extreme cases in the past, bombings. Many dispute the applicability of the term "violence" to describe destruction of property, since they argue that destruction of property is done not to control an individual or institution but to take its control away.

The issue of authenticity is important in this subculture—the pejorative term ''Reconexionista'' ("re-connectionist") is applied to those who associate with desconexión and adopt its stylistic attributes but are deemed not to share or understand the underlying values or philosophy.

